# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch H."""
DESC_H = {
    "PT": {
        0: "The pilot of Mazinger Z.\nHe is a hot-blooded young man with a strong sense of justice, though simple-minded and a bit careless. Entrusted with Mazinger Z by his grandfather, Dr. Juzo Kabuto, he went into battle to crush the ambitions of the evil scientist Dr. Hell, who sought world domination.\nAt first he had no idea how to operate the robot and piloted it recklessly, but the skills he had honed riding motorcycles and his natural talent for close combat soon became second nature to him in the cockpit. Those abilities served him well in hand-to-hand fighting against the Iron Mask forces as well.\nAfter wiping out Dr. Hell's army of Mechanical Beasts, he entrusted the fight against the new threat of the Mycenae Empire to Tetsuya Tsurugi and Great Mazinger, and left for the United States to study abroad. However, as the Mycenae Empire's assaults intensified, he returned home for a time and helped bring about the enemy's defeat.\nAfter finishing his studies abroad and returning to Japan, he threw himself into the fight against the Vega Star Alliance alongside Duke Fleed, piloting the TFO he had built himself and the newly developed Double Spazer.",
        1: "The daughter of Professor Yumi, director of the Photon Power Laboratory, and the pilot of Aphrodite A and Diana A.\nCheerful by nature, she is quite skilled at piloting both robots and motorcycles. She also has a tomboyish streak, which sometimes got her into trouble.\nShe and Kouji often butted heads, but through repeated clashes they built a bond of trust and became what could be called the best of partners.\nAfter the fight against Dr. Hell's army of Mechanical Beasts ended, she went to study in the United States together with Kouji.",
        2: "Kouji's younger brother.\nA kind and cheerful boy who always worries about Kouji while also cheering him on. At times, though, he shows a mischievous streak much like his brother's.\nHe is well liked, with many friends both at the Photon Power Laboratory and at school.\nIn 'Great Mazinger', it was revealed that Kenzo Kabuto, director of the Science Fortress Institute, is his father. The two of them awkwardly worked to make up for the years they had lost.",
        3: "Director of the Photon Power Laboratory.\nHe is Dr. Juzo Kabuto's top disciple, entrusted with full authority over the laboratory. He seems to have earned complete trust, having even been told of Dr. Hell's ambitions.\nHe is the foremost authority on Photon Power and Super Alloy Z research, and developed Mazinger Z's new weapons as well as Aphrodite A and Diana A.\nIn battle, he gave Kouji and Sayaka cautious but precise instructions, proving his worth as a combat commander as well.",
        4: "One of the three scientists who assist Professor Yumi at the Photon Power Laboratory.\nQuiet by nature, he approaches every problem carefully and deliberately. Working alongside Dr. Sewashi and the late Dr. Morimori, he helped develop Mazinger Z's additional weapons as well as Boss Borot.",
        5: "One of the three scientists who assist Professor Yumi at the Photon Power Laboratory, and something of a leader among them.\nShort-tempered by nature, but a first-rate scientist. Working alongside Dr. Nossori and the late Dr. Morimori, he helped develop Mazinger Z's additional weapons as well as Boss Borot.",
        6: "The pilot of Great Mazinger. Eighteen years old.\nHe grew up in an orphanage until Dr. Kenzo Kabuto took him in so that he could pilot Great Mazinger. Raised from then on with combat drilled into him, he became a top-class fighter and pilot. Outside of battle, however, his poor way with words tends to leave people with an impression of him as rough and unrefined.\nHe looked after Shiro as if he were his own younger brother and built a bond of trust with Boss and the others, becoming the pillar of the Mazinger team in place of Kouji, who had gone to America.",
        7: "Tetsuya's support pilot and the pilot of Venus A.\nShe grew up in an orphanage until Dr. Kenzo Kabuto took her in and raised her as a warrior in preparation for the coming battle with the Mycenae Empire. Having grown up together with Tetsuya, she became a good partner to him.\nTrue to her name, she has a fierce, fiery temperament, being both spirited and unwilling to lose. Though she usually puts up a strong front, she harbors a complex about her own birth and has been known to brood over it.",
        8: "Kouji's classmate at Toujo Academy and the pilot of Boss Borot. He is always accompanied by his followers Nuke and Mucha.\nA show-off and a flatterer who is exactly as simple-minded as he looks. He is hopeless around pretty women, getting far more excited than necessary and going weak in the knees whenever a female guest appears. Naturally, he is smitten with both Sayaka and Jun.\nHe harbors intense rivalry toward Kouji, and out of a desire for a robot of his own to shine in, he kidnapped the Photon Power Laboratory's three scientists and forced them to build Boss Borot.\nThough he always clowns around, he has a genuine desire to protect peace. Fighting alongside Kouji and Tetsuya, even if he sometimes got in their way, he built a deep friendship and bond of trust with them.",
        9: "One of Boss's followers.\nThe most easygoing of the three, known for his slow, drawn-out way of speaking.",
        10: "One of Boss's followers.\nAlways full of energy, he serves as the group's mood-maker.",
        11: "The identity Duke Fleed assumes while active on Earth.\nOrdinarily he helps out at Shirakaba Ranch. But the moment the Vega Star Alliance appears, he dons his combat suit with a cry of \"Duke Fleed!\" and sorties as a warrior.",
        12: "The pilot of Grendizer.\nHe is the prince of Planet Fleed, destroyed by the Vega Star Alliance, and one of its few survivors. A kind-hearted young man who wishes for peace and believes in love and friendship, he possesses great physical ability along with various psychic powers, including telepathy.\nHaving fled the Vega Star Alliance and made his way to Earth, he began a new life as Daisuke, son of Dr. Umon. But upon learning that the Vega Star Alliance had set its sights on Earth, he resolved to fight in Grendizer to protect his second home.",
        13: "Danbei's daughter.\nA cheerful, spirited girl with the athletic ability to handle horseback riding with ease.\nShe gradually fell for Daisuke, who worked at the ranch her father managed. After learning that his true identity was the alien Duke Fleed, she resolved without hesitation to fight alongside him. In time she became the pilot of the Marine Spazer, supporting Duke both in battle and in daily life. Her cheerfulness seems to have been a source of comfort for Duke, who carried a dark past.",
        14: "Duke's younger sister and princess of Planet Fleed. Fourteen years old.\nWhen Planet Fleed was attacked by the Vega Star Alliance, she barely escaped but became separated from Duke, fleeing to Earth together with an elderly attendant.\nAt first she mistook Duke for an enemy, but upon seeing the royal pendant she became certain he was her brother, and the two reconciled. From then on she mainly rode in the Drill Spazer, joining forces with him to fight the Vega Star Alliance.",
        15: "Director of the Space Science Institute.\nA brilliant scientist specializing in the study of UFOs and space science. To bolster the power of Grendizer, which could not be enhanced through Earth science alone, he developed several external augmentation devices such as the Double Spazer and the Cosmo Special.\nHe is also a big-hearted man, having rescued the alien Duke Fleed and taken him in as his own son.\nDuring the fight against the Vega Star Alliance, he served as a combat commander, giving calm and precise instructions to support Daisuke and the Grendizer team.",
        16: "The head of Shirakaba Ranch and father of Hikaru and Goro.\nHis hobby is sky watching, in hopes of spotting a UFO and encountering aliens.",
        17: "Hikaru's younger brother.\nA mischievous but cheerful and honest boy who looks up to Daisuke like an older brother.",
        18: "The absolute ruler of Planet Vega and holder of full authority over the Vega Star Alliance.\nHe plots to rule the entire universe, invading other planets by force and destroying every world that dared resist, Planet Fleed among them.\nHe remains on Planet Vega himself, issuing orders for the invasion of Earth to Skull Moon, the forward base built on the Moon.",
        19: "The officer in charge of Skull Moon, the forward base the Vega Star Alliance built on the Moon, and supreme commander of the invasion of Earth.\nHe has sworn absolute loyalty to Emperor Vega and strives to carry out his orders faithfully, favoring a style of combat that crushes the enemy through sheer force.\nHidden within him is a female personality of the opposite temperament, named 'Lady Gandal,' who favors scheming and treachery. When she speaks up, Gandal's face splits in two to reveal her as a small woman. Later, after Gandal suffered a facial injury, he underwent surgery so that his face could switch between the two personalities.",
        20: "Emperor Vega's daughter, and also Duke's betrothed.\nAs a child, she was sent to Planet Fleed as part of a political arrangement, and she had loved Duke ever since that time.",
        21: "Having previously piloted the Eagle - Getter 1, he now pilots the Dragon - Getter Dragon. Eighteen years old.\nA student at Asama Academy, he can be a bit inflexible but is serious and single-minded by nature. He serves as captain of the soccer team and, as the leader of the Getter Team, keeps its three pilots working together.\nHis family runs a kendo dojo in Kyushu, and he often drew on the swordsmanship his father drilled into him from an early age when fighting. At times he even faced members of the Hyakki Hundred in unarmed combat.\nHe seems to be popular not only with the girls at his school but also with Gola of the Dinosaur Empire (Miyuki Saotome) and Kochouki of the Hyakki Empire, making him quite the heartbreaker even though he has no such intentions himself.",
        22: "Having previously piloted the Jaguar - Getter 2, he now pilots the Liger - Getter Liger. Eighteen years old.\nA student at Asama Academy, he is the only member of the Getter Team not in an athletic club, despite having outstanding physical reflexes.\nAt first, his overconfidence made him keep others at a distance, a constant source of friction within the team. But as he built a bond of trust with Ryouma and the others through battle, he began to take things more seriously, and his calm judgment saved the Getter Team from crisis time and again.\nThe cross he always wears is a keepsake from his late mother, who is said to have borne a faint resemblance to Michiru, and it holds her photograph inside.",
        23: "He joined the Getter Team in place of Musashi, who died in battle, and pilots the Poseidon - Getter Poseidon. Eighteen years old.\nA transfer student to Asama Academy, he joined the Getter Team on the strength of his monstrous power, enough to flatten dozens of athletes at once, and a toughness impressive enough that he could doze off even while riding the Getter training simulator.\nHis hobby is baseball, and he later became captain of Asama Academy's baseball team. His pilot suit reflects this, looking every bit like a baseball uniform.\nA pacifist who dislikes fighting, he even turned down piloting Getter for a time. But he is fond of children and kind-hearted at heart, as shown when he rallied himself to fight after Genki was captured by a Hyakki mecha.",
        24: "Dr. Saotome's daughter.\nLike Ryouma and the others, she attends Asama Academy, and her cheerful, kind nature has made her so popular that she is called the Mona Lisa of Asama Academy. She was something of a Madonna figure to the Getter Team as well.\nSwitching from the Command Machine to the Lady Command, she skillfully supported the Getter Team from behind the lines with reconnaissance, supply runs, and covering fire, becoming indispensable in battle. During the final battle, she piloted Getter Liger to fill the gap left by Hayato's absence.",
        25: "Director of the Saotome Institute and father of Michiru and Genki.\nWith his unshaven face, wooden sandals, and perpetually messy office, he makes an unimpressive first impression. But he is the foremost authority on the mysterious cosmic radiation known as 'Getter Rays,' and his ability as a scientist is recognized as world-class.\nThough he originally developed Getter Robo for space exploration, when the Dinosaur Empire suddenly appeared he armed Getter and used it to defend the Earth. He later completed a new combat-model Getter Robo to fight the Hyakki Empire as well.\nIn battle he also served as a commander, never losing his composure even in the direst moments, and his sound judgment made him a great pillar of support for the Getter Team.",
        26: "Dr. Saotome's second son.\nTrue to his name, he is an energetic and mischievous elementary school boy. Never shy around strangers, he quickly warmed up to Benkei after his later arrival and treated him like a friend.\nHe even became friendly with Jimushiki, a boy from the Hyakki Empire, and his active nature helped the Getter Team on more than one occasion.",
        27: "The emperor who rules the Hyakki Empire, possessing powerful telepathic abilities.\nThe Hyakki Empire's goal is to implant artificial horns that serve as telepathic receiver antennae into people's heads, turning humanity into Hyakki soldiers to use as pawns for world conquest. But efficiently developing Hyakki soldiers and Hyakki mecha requires a Getter Ray amplifier, and Burai has relentlessly attacked the Saotome Institute in order to obtain one.\nHe possesses the ruthlessness, cruelty, and majesty one would expect from his demonic appearance, exceeding even those of Emperor Gore, ruler of the Dinosaur Empire.\nYet he can also show leniency toward his subordinates. When he learned that Hakkotsuki's daughter Lisa had betrayed them, he honored Hakkotsuki's plea not to have to kill his own daughter and ordered someone else to carry out the execution instead. He also showed consideration for Hidler, who had just made a miraculous return from the brink of death before the final battle, by ordering him to rest.",
        28: "The combat commander who oversees the Hyakki Empire's military might. Along with Dr. Gura, he serves as one of Emperor Burai's right-hand men, but behind the scenes he is a scheming man with his eye on Burai's own position.\nUnderhanded and contemptible by nature, he directs his malice at ally and enemy alike. In the past, fearing that his position as marshal was threatened, he framed General Jirai and had him executed, and when he judged that the general's son Jiraiki had likewise become a threat, he treacherously struck him down amid the fighting.\nHe is no mere petty villain, however; he possesses real ability, having broken through the barrier of the newly built battleship Sea Force with his personal fighter craft, survived the explosion of a Hyakki robot against all odds, and even taken Hayato prisoner while making his escape.",
        29: "The scientist who serves as the brains of the Hyakki Empire, working alongside Marshal Hidler as one of Emperor Burai's right-hand men.\nHe is responsible for developing Hyakki mecha and fighter craft as well as drafting strategy, and his brilliant mind is indispensable to the Hyakki Empire.\nTalented young members such as Jimushiki and Tekkoki gathered under him, learning from him day after day.",
        30: "One of the Hyakki Hundred, the elite corps of the Hyakki Empire.\nSupremely confident in his own intellect, he developed the Hyakki mecha Mecha Tekkoki himself and used it to challenge Getter Robo.\nHis combat ability was also first-rate, skillful enough to fight Getter Robo to a standstill and beyond. But when Hidler's tank forced its way into the battle, his pride was wounded, and he turned his blade on Hidler to protect Getter Robo. Then, battered and bloodied, he challenged Getter to a fair rematch.",
        31: "One of the Hyakki Hundred, the elite corps of the Hyakki Empire.\nHe had been transforming dam workers and security guards into Hyakki soldiers, and after his predecessor Ikkakuki fell to Getter Robo, he took over the plan to steal the Getter Ray amplifier.\nMaking use of his Hyakki robot's special traits, he attempted to attack the Saotome Institute by tunneling up from underground.",
        32: "A veteran warrior among the Hyakki Hundred, the elite corps of the Hyakki Empire.\nOnce so formidable that he was called a hero of the skies, he had retired from active duty in his old age. But when Hidler lied to him that his son Gyuugaki had been killed by Getter Robo, he resolved to seek revenge.\nEven in old age his skill had not faded, and his battle-hardened prowess put the Getter Team through real hardship.",
        33: "The pilot of KuRaiOh and main pilot of God Sigma. Eighteen years old.\nA man who loved space, believed in the future, and fought single-mindedly for peace. Though he comes from Io, he speaks with the brisk, plainspoken manner of a true Edokko, a native of old Tokyo, and he is warmhearted, spirited, and hot-blooded, never one to fuss over small details.\nOn Io, he had experience helping build an ionium refinery using mining robots, giving him an edge when it comes to piloting machinery. Even KuRaiOh, which he boarded in an emergency during an Elder attack, he handled as naturally as his own limbs.\nHe is also a formidable fighter unarmed, and his jumping kick in particular packs a fierce punch.\nThough he and Teral, the Elder commander, are enemies, Toshiya seems to sense something in him not unlike himself.",
        34: "The pilot of KaiMeiOh. Twenty-one years old.\nAn extremely cool-headed and sharp-tongued man, whose too-accurate observations often stir up trouble. At heart, though, he is honest and straightforward - his foul mouth is simply his way of covering up an inability to be candid.\nHe also serves as chief engineer at Trinity Base and is the second-sharpest mind there after Dr. Kazami. A hard worker, he has made it his goal to one day surpass Dr. Kazami himself.\nHis attachment to money runs strong enough to seem miserly, though there appears to be some deeper reason behind it.",
        35: "The pilot of RikuShinOh.\nHe lost both parents before his own eyes in an Elder attack, yet his bright, straightforward personality shows none of that tragedy. That said, he is also a flatterer, a show-off, and something of a daredevil. Perhaps because they are close in maturity, he gets along especially well with Rie's younger brother Shouta, who looks up to him like an older brother.\nHopeless with machines by nature, he could not even handle RikuShinOh well at first. But when he learned that God Sigma could be formed and that KuRaiOh would be its main unit, he pushed Toshiya aside and climbed into KuRaiOh himself. KuRaiOh's onboard computer, however, declared as a piloting requirement, \"Fighting spirit alone is not enough. A calm mind and trained skill are required,\" making him painfully aware of what he lacked. From then on, through sheer grit, he gradually managed to get the hang of at least RikuShinOh.",
        36: "Dr. Kazami's stepdaughter and secretary.\nAn exceptionally gifted young woman, she skillfully supported Dr. Kazami to keep Trinity Base's wide-ranging operations running smoothly.\nShe had been living apart from her younger brother Shouta, but the two later came to live together inside the base.\nShe secretly harbors feelings for Toshiya, and keeps a photograph of him displayed in her room.\nIn place of Dr. Kazami, who opposed sending Trinity Base to Jupiter until the very end, she came to take full command of the base after its departure.",
        37: "Martino's daughter.\nAs her high-fashion sense suggests, she is overconfident and willful, the type to do whatever she pleases.\nShe calls herself Toshiya's girlfriend and is a rival to Rie.\nShe is also a troublemaker, repeatedly acting on her own impulses in ways that both create and resolve crises for God Sigma.",
        38: "The financial backer of Trinity City.\nA self-centered man obsessed with money, who judges every action solely by whether it will turn a profit. This is plain enough from the fact that, even in the midst of the Elder invasion, he tried to sell off KuRaiOh, KaiMeiOh, and RikuShinOh.\nYet his love for his daughter Minako runs deep, and he treasures her just as much as his money.",
        39: "The genius scientist who developed both Trinity Energy, said to be phase energy extracted from a distortion in dimensional space, and God Sigma itself.\nGentle and tolerant by nature, he took in the orphaned Rie and treats Toshiya and the others with the same warmth as a parent. His keen mind also makes him a capable battle commander, and he serves as the spiritual pillar of Trinity Base.",
        40: "The supreme commander leading the Elder forces.\nHe was dispatched to Earth's past under orders from the Elder Council to seize Trinity Energy.\nHe commands the absolute trust of his two lieutenants and his many subordinates, seeking to accomplish his mission through unity. However, he runs into unexpectedly fierce resistance from God Sigma, throwing his plans badly off course.\nWhen sending out two of his subordinates who are lovers, he gives them especially strong encouragement and even looks after them afterward, and he is visibly moved by the way his enemies Toshiya and Rie disregard their own safety for each other's sake. He has a soft spot for men and women who care for one another, revealing at times a somewhat feminine side.",
        41: "The woman whose spirit now resides within Teral.\nOriginally Teral's lover, she was aboard a battleship struck by an attack from Earth's forces in the future; Teral shielded her from the blast, but he was buried beneath the falling debris and died.\nVowing both revenge against the Earth that had torn them apart and to spend her whole life together with her beloved Teral, she used a special procedure to fuse her own spirit with Teral's body.",
        42: "An Elder military commander under Teral, responsible for developing the Cosmosaurus.\nHe is devoted to Teral, and his efforts to seize Trinity Energy seem driven less by loyalty to his homeland than by devotion to Teral himself.\nHe and his colleague Ritsu are on famously bad terms, but he has the flexibility to work with him willingly whenever it is for Teral's sake.",
        43: "An Elder military commander under Teral.\nA fierce warrior, he clashes with God Sigma again and again in pursuit of Trinity Energy for the sake of his homeland and Teral. Yet he is in constant conflict with Jira, who develops the Cosmosaurus so vital to their operations. Even so, when Teral is in danger, the two set aside their usual bickering and work together in perfect sync.\nHe serves Teral with unwavering loyalty as his subject, and has even risked his own life to save him from danger.",
        44: "A soldier who came from the Elder homeworld ostensibly to assist Teral.\nExtremely cunning and ruthless, he will use any means necessary to achieve his ends. He did not come to the present era to save his homeworld Elder, but rather to seize Trinity Energy, depose the Elder Council, and rule Elder himself.\nTo that end, Teral's presence is an obstacle, and Gagarn has employed various schemes to undermine him. He once stormed Teral's base, forcing a situation where Teral had no choice but to fight back, then destroyed the base and claimed it had been \"self-defense.\" Within the base as well, he ruled Teral's soldiers with an iron fist, and eventually ousted Teral to take the position of supreme commander of the invasion of Earth.\nHe is no mere villain, however; his abilities are considerable. Leading a fleet into battle or piloting the giant robot Gargos, he overwhelmed God Sigma from start to finish. He also possesses a sharp eye for observation, having seen through Teral's true nature even when Teral's own direct subordinates Ritsu and Jira had not.\nHe keeps as a pet a Lotbird, a creature both strikingly colorful and formidable in combat.",
        45: "Gagarn's lieutenant and combat commander.\nWith his red skin, harsh scowl, powerful build, and overbearing manner, he cuts an intimidating figure. His true character, though, is far less impressive: extremely bold whenever he has the upper hand, but instantly reduced to cowardice the moment things turn against him.",
        46: "Gagarn's lieutenant and chief of science.\nHe creates new models of the Cosmosaurus and devises operations that make use of them.\nHis brilliant mind earns him recognition even from Gagarn, who relies on him as a right-hand man. Yet he seems to regard betrayal as a virtue, having switched his allegiance to Teral not once but twice.",
    },
}
